Summary : Error 401 Unauthorized when sending a public GET /users/{id} request after successful user registration

Component : Users / Authentication

Severity : High

Priority : High

Steps to Reproduce :

1.Open Postman and send a POST request to create a user:
https://api.practicesoftwaretesting.com/users/register
Request body (JSON):
{
  "first_name": "Tony",
  "last_name": "Stark",
  "phone": "1234567890",
  "dob": "1970-05-29",
  "password": "TonyStark_M4_2026_!!#",
  "email": "stark_iron_boss_2026@stark.com", 
  "address": {
    "street": "Malibu Point",
    "house_number": "10800",
    "city": "Los Angeles",
    "state": "California",
    "country": "USA",
    "postal_code": "90265"
  }
}
2.Make sure that the response status is 201 Created and copy the generated user ID (01ksj2y5kc93dkeq7k8xserhzh)

3.Create a new GET request to retrieve data by ID:
https://api.practicesoftwaretesting.com/users/01ksj2y5kc93dkeq7k8xserhzh

4.In the Authorization tab, select the No Auth value (the request is sent without a token)

5.Click the Send button

Actual Result : 
The server returns the 401 Unauthorized status code. Access to data is blocked

Expected Result : 

The request is successful, and the server returns a 200 OK status code and JSON data for the user profile. The GET /users/{id} endpoint must be public, since the authorization token is not returned in the response body during registration (POST /users/register)
